implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (DoD 2). Append one test, C6, at the end of moe-vscode/tests/settings-policy-corpus.test.cjs. Use the session's own editing tool (Claude Edit/Write, or apply_patch on a codex exec seat). Never use a shell write or a subagent: either leaves no TOOL witness and the path is HELD at landing.

Reuse the file's existing rowsOf() (effectivePolicyRows → worktreeLandingRow → worktreeTarget, transpiled into a vm). Add no new harness. Write it as:

test('C6: in worktree mode a consolidationBranch holding *, ? or [ lands on main; any other branch, ] included, lands as written', () => {
    const landing = consolidationBranch => rowsOf({ worktreeMode: 'on', consolidationBranch }).find(row => row.label === 'Landing branch');
    const glob = 'A glob consolidationBranch is not a landing target; each completion lands on main.';
    const literal = 'Each completion lands as one merge-tree squash commit on this branch.';
    for (const branch of ['moe/work-*', 'release/v?', 'release/[ab]', '[']) {
        assert.deepStrictEqual(landing(branch), { label: 'Landing branch', value: 'main', detail: glob }, branch);
    }
    for (const branch of ['release/train', 'release/a]b', 'feature/x-1']) {
        assert.deepStrictEqual(landing(branch), { label: 'Landing branch', value: branch, detail: literal }, branch);
    }
});

Why it is needed: the shared corpus pins only `*` in worktree mode (row P14). A lint "fix" that drops ? or [ from the class, or adds ], would still pass C1-C5.

The change is behavior-neutral, so C6 passes on the unfixed base too. It is a regression pin, not a red test. Leave the corpus JSON moe-jetbrains/src/test/resources/client-settings-policy.json alone: JetBrains replays the same corpus, and this file's header says the corpus is only read here.

tests/*.cjs are not linted (`eslint src --ext ts`), so this file does not affect DoD 1. See mem:gotcha-vscode-settings-panel-test-patterns.
